[ti:Day 02]

[00:00.00]implicit [ɪmˈplɪsɪt]a. 含蓄的；内含的；隐性的；无疑问 的；无保留的 例 In our work, we judge using the implicit models our intuition provides.
[00:12.36]hasty [ˈheɪsti]a. 匆忙的，仓促的；草率的 例 Faced with emergency, some people are prone to jump to hasty conclusions.
[00:23.16]helm [helm]n. 舵；舵柄；掌管 vt. 给…掌舵；指挥 例 Apple's executive team hoped the first device sold without their visionary leader at the helm would protect them against a growing challenge from the likes of Samsung Electronics. 搭 at the helm of 掌管着 / take the helm of 开 始掌管
[00:48.96]mind-boggling [ˈmaɪndbɒɡlɪŋ]a. 难以理解的；令人惊异的，令 人难以置信的 例 He created mind-boggling effects with his computer.
[01:00.24]insurrection [ˌɪnsəˈrekʃn]n. 暴动；叛乱；起义；造反 搭 armed insurrection 武装起义
[01:07.44]cellular [ˈseljələ(r)]a. 细胞的；蜂窝状的；网眼的；箱格 式的 搭 cellular structure 细胞结构
[01:14.88]overhead [ˈəʊvəhed]a. 头上的；架空的；管理用的；经费 的 n. 间接费用；[pl.] 日常开支；管理费用
[01:21.72]expiration [ˌekspəˈreɪʃn]n. 结束，终止；期满
[01:25.80]wanted [ˈwɒntɪd]a. 被征求的；受通缉的
[01:28.92]suitability [ˌsuːtəˈbɪləti]n. 合适；适用；适合性
[01:33.36]inelastic [ˌɪnɪˈlæstɪk]a. 无弹性的；不能变通的；不能适应 的 例 Our clients have an inelastic demand for products.
[01:43.44]supervise [ˈsuːpəvaɪz]vt. 监督，管理；指导 例 The investment data of foreign capital enterprises are checked and supervised by the industrial and commercial administration management sectors.
[02:02.64]gravitate [ˈɡrævɪteɪt]vi. 下跌，下降；受重力作用；受吸 引；移向 vt. 使受…吸引 例 Both beginners and experts tend over time to gravitate towards intermediates. 搭 gravitate to/towards 被吸引到
[02:19.68]conflict [ˈkɒnflɪkt]n. 冲突；矛盾，争执；斗争 [kənˈflɪkt]vi. 斗争；冲突；抵触 例 The conflict between management and workers makes for inefficiency in the workplace. 搭 conflict of... 关于…的冲突 / in conflict with 与…相冲突；和…不一致
[02:40.56]exaggerate [ɪɡˈzædʒəreɪt]v. (使)夸张，(使)夸大 例 Tell your manager the exact difficulties of your work, neither exaggerate nor conceal.
[02:54.00]chip [tʃɪp]n. 芯片；(作赌注或讨价还价用的)筹码；钱 例 The stock will move further up as functionality starts to consolidate from the board to the chip. 搭 cash in one's chip 把筹码兑成现金 / in the chips 有钱，富有
[03:12.24]reckon [ˈrekən]v. 计算；测算 搭 reckon up 结算；估价 / reckon with 和…算 账；处理；对付
[03:18.96]recession [rɪˈseʃn]n. (经济的)衰退；衰退期；撤回，退回
[03:23.40]foregone [ˈfɔːɡɒn]a. 先前的，过去的；预知的 例 The election result is not a foregone conclusion.
[03:32.16]camcorder [ˈkæmkɔːdə(r)]n. 便携式摄像机 例 All of the camcorder's main components come in pairs: two lenses, two image sensors and two image processors.
[03:47.04]hunter [ˈhʌntə(r)]n. 猎人；猎犬；搜寻者，追逐者 例 Prior to the purchase decision, the hunter has a thorough understanding of specific needs and the issues affecting the decision- making.
[04:04.92]troubleshooter [ˈtrʌblʃuːtə(r)]n. 故障检修工；纷争解决者；调解 人
[04:10.56]cancellation [ˌkænsəˈleɪʃn]n. 注销；取消，撤销；抵消，对消 例 The cancellation of the summit marks an escalation in tensions between America and some European countries.
[04:26.76]bug [bʌɡ]n. 故障；名流，要人 例 Your job is to have the seriousness of the bug accurately assessed. 搭 big bug 大人物；大错误 / bug check 出错检 查
[04:39.00]original [əˈrɪdʒənl]a. 最初的，原先的；原创的；独创的 n. 原物；原创 例 The statue is a reproduction, not the original.
[04:49.08]benchmark [ˈbentʃmɑːk]n. 基准，基准尺度；标杆；用于比 较分析的基本性资料 例 Now the region's benchmark index has plunged to its lowest level in over the last two years.
[05:03.84]accumulate [əˈkjuːmjəleɪt]v. 积累，积聚；堆积 例 Most countries have accumulated an impressive stock of hard-currency reserves.
[05:16.44]costing [ˈkɒstɪŋ]n. 成本核算 例 It provides a new method to improve traditional costing accounting by cost driver analysis.
[05:28.56]shaky [ˈʃeɪki]a. 虚弱的；不稳定的；不可靠的；摇晃的
[05:32.40]amenity [əˈmiːnəti]n. [常pl.]生活福利设施；(环境、气候 等)舒适，宜人；礼仪 例 Nap rooms have become a more commonplace amenity for companies looking to bill themselves as fun, dynamic places to work. 搭 exchange of amenities 寒暄
[05:53.28]core [kɔː(r)]n. 核心；精髓；中心；芯线 例 Management of succession must be at the core of how you manage the company. 搭 core city 市中心 / to the core 彻底地
[06:06.84]distinguish [dɪˈstɪŋɡwɪʃ]vt. 区分，辨别；使杰出；使突出 例 Manufactures are striving to distinguish their products in terms of quality, unit price and added-value features. 搭 distinguish between…and… 把…和…区分开 来 / distinguish oneself 使杰出
[06:30.00]factual [ˈfæktʃuəl]a. 事实的；实际的；真实的；确实的 例 Securities trading information disseminated by all media must be factual and objective and not misleading.
[06:45.36]infringe [ɪnˈfrɪndʒ]vt. 破坏；侵犯；违犯 vi. 侵犯 例 The measures that the government has taken may infringe on privacy and civil liberties. 搭 infringe upon sb's right 侵犯某人的权利
[07:02.04]virtue [ˈvɜːtʃuː]n. 美德，德行；优点，长处；功效，效 力 例 By virtue of being a multinational enterprise for a decade, the company has accumulated $9.2 billion in corporate assets. 搭 by virtue of 凭借…的力量；由于
[07:21.12]well-off [ˌwelˈɒf]a. 富裕的；供应充足的；繁荣昌盛的 搭 be well-off for …供应充足
[07:27.48]toss [tɒs]vi. 掷钱币作决定；辗转 vt. 投掷；使不安； 谈论 n. 摇摆；掷钱币决定的事 例 My little brother and I often toss to see who pays the bill. 搭 toss for sth. 掷钱币以决定某事
[07:41.16]ascertain [ˌæsəˈteɪn]vt. 弄清，查明；确定 例 We must ascertain the responsibility in light of different situations.
[07:52.32]defray [dɪˈfreɪ]vt. 支付 例 Most transportation companies announced fare increases to defray increases in fuel prices.
[08:04.32]announce [əˈnaʊns]v. 宣布，宣告；诉说；预示；播报 例 We expect to announce more partnerships in the near future. 搭 announce amnesty 宣布赦免
[08:16.80]patronise [ˈpætrənaɪz]vt. 资助；惠顾；以高人一等的态度 对待(别人) 例 Unlike other colleagues in the company, he does not patronise newbies.
[08:29.40]skyrocket [ˈskaɪrɒkɪt]v. (使)猛涨，(使)猛升 例 Many citizens worry prices will continue to skyrocket.
[08:39.24]teleprompter [ ˈteliprɒmptə(r)]n. 讲话提示机；提词器
[08:44.04]accident [ˈæksɪdənt]n. 意外事件，事故；意外因素
[08:48.00]emergency [iˈmɜːdʒənsi]n. 紧急情况，突发事件；非常时刻 a. 紧急的；备用的 搭 emergency medical technician 急诊医生 / in case of emergency 在紧急情况下，以防万一 / proclaim a state of emergency 宣布处于紧急状 态
[09:04.92]climax [ˈklaɪmæks]n. 高峰；顶点；高潮 例 With the opening of the exhibition, various products are beginning to reach the sales climax.
[09:17.76]hammer [ˈhæmə(r)]n. 锤，铁榔头 vi. 捶打 vt. 捶击；使成 例 All of the staff in the company are working hammer and tongs to raise productivity. 搭 hammer and tongs 全力以赴地；拼命地 / hammer away 致力于 / hammer out 锤成；设 计出
[09:36.96]jobbing [ˈdʒɒbɪŋ]a. 做零工的；做散工的 例 Our customers are globally located, ranging from multinationals to small jobbing centres.
[09:49.68]galaxy [ˈɡæləksi]n. 星系；[the G -] 银河(系)；一群(杰 出的人)；一批(美好的事物) 例 Astronomers have detected a planet at least the size of Jupiter and they believe it is in another galaxy. 搭 a galaxy of 一群 / galaxy clustering 星系成 团 / galaxy evolution 星系演化
[10:12.84]sabotage [ˈsæbətɑːʒ]n. 怠工；暗中破坏 vt. 从事破坏活 动；妨害 搭 sabotage on 对…进行破坏
[10:19.68]achievement [əˈtʃiːvmənt]n. 成就，成绩；达到，完成，实现 例 The achievement of her purpose mainly depends on her perseverance.
[10:31.44]ideology [ˌaɪdiˈɒlədʒi]n. 意识形态，思维方式；观念学 例 His biggest weakness has to do with ideology rather than age.
[10:42.12]modest [ˈmɒdɪst]a. 普通的；适中的；适当的；不过分的 例 There is a modest improvement in housing conditions for the company's employees.
[10:54.48]compliment [ˈkɒmplɪmənt]n. 赞美(话)，恭维(话) [ˈkɒmplɪment]vt. 称赞，恭维 例 After the party, you should compliment the host to show your gratitude. 搭 compliment away 赠送，把…作为赠品散发 / compliment sb. out of sth. 恭维某人以骗取某物 / pay a compliment to sb. on sth. 因某事赞美 某人
[11:19.56]unchecked [ˌʌnˈtʃekt]a. 未受制止的；未经检查的 例 China's economic situation is set to become dangerous if its house prices continue to rise unchecked.
[11:33.96]psychometric [ˌsaɪkəˈmetrɪk]a. 心理测试的 搭 psychometric test 心理测验
[11:40.56]stockpile [ˈstɒkpaɪl]n. (原料、食品等的)储备；(备用原料 或物资的)贮存 vt. 大量贮备 例 The present stockpile of unsold houses will be enough for millions of citizens.
[11:55.08]arrangement [əˈreɪndʒmənt]n. [常pl.] 安排，准备工作；整 理；排列；布置 例 He has made every arrangement to meet any emergency. 搭 make arrangements 做安排
[12:08.76]fiduciary [fɪˈdjuːʃəri]a. 信用的；受信托的；(纸币)信用发 行的 n. 被信托者，受托人 例 The risks in these deals are so uncontrollable that if a deal went wrong, the PE firm would be vulnerable to a lawsuit by its partners for breach of fiduciary duty.
[12:31.20]mat [mæt]n. 席子；垫子 v. (使)缠结 a. 毛的；不光 滑的 例 The hi-tech product is a mat made of an electronic screen. 搭 on the mat 受责备；受审问
[12:42.72]approve [əˈpruːv]vt. 批准；表示认可，同意；赞成 vi. 赞 成；满意 例 To achieve all this, the national governments must approve some 300 directives. 搭 approve sb. of doing sth. 赞成某人做某事
[12:59.28]systematic [ˌsɪstəˈmætɪk]a. 有系统的；系统性的；有规则 的；彻底的
[13:04.56]waybill [weɪˈbɪl]n. 乘客名单；运货单
[13:07.68]scalper [ˈskælpə(r)]n. (以买卖股票等)套利者；黄牛党
[13:12.00]quality [ˈkwɒləti]n. 质量；品质；特性；身份，地位 a. 优质的，高级的 搭 in the quality of 以…身份(资格) / quality of life 生活品质
[13:21.96]inject [ɪnˈdʒekt]vt. 注入 例 Reform of this system would inject more vitality into the Chinese economy.
[13:32.16]trundle [ˈtrʌndl]n. 小车轮；滚动 vt. 使滚动；(以车辆)载 运，运送 vi. 滚动；慢步前行；重提某事 例 The negotiation has been trundling on for weeks and there's still no end in sight.
[13:47.16]invalidate [ɪnˈvælɪdeɪt]vt. 使无效；使作废
[13:51.12]apprehend [ˌæprɪˈhend]v. 逮捕，拘押；领会，理解；疑惧， 担心 例 The police investigate a crime and may apprehend suspects and detain them in custody. 搭 imperfectly apprehend 理解不完全；一知半 解
[14:08.40]premise [ˈpremɪs]n. 前提；[pl.] 上述事项；房屋(及其附 属建筑、地基等)；生产经营场所 搭 on the premise of 在…的前提下 / on the premises (尤指酒店)在场所内
[14:20.04]cross [krɒs]vt. 勾销；划掉 a. 相反的；不利的；相互 的；交叉的 例 Write the number next to the item name, and cross it off your work list. 搭 get sth. on the cross 〈口〉用不正当手段获 得某物
[14:35.16]rapport [ræˈpɔː(r)]n. 和睦，融洽；关系密切 例 It is necessary to nurture emotional rapport between your brand and its followers. 搭 in rapport with 与…关系密切
[14:49.68]rapprochement [ræˈprɒʃmɒ]n. 恢复邦交；和睦；亲善 例 There is no obvious sign of rapprochement between the two countries.
[15:01.08]adversarial [ˌædvəˈseəriəl]a. 敌对的；对抗性的 搭 adversarial relationship 敌对关系 / adversarial system 抗辩式诉讼制度
[15:11.76]reiterate [riˈɪtəreɪt]vt. 反复说；反复做；重申 搭 reiterate one's view 重申己见
[15:18.60]humiliate [hjuːˈmɪlieɪt]vt. 使蒙羞，使丢脸；羞辱 例 There is no reason for you to humiliate our former competitors and present friends. 搭 humiliate oneself 丢脸；出丑
[15:34.08]ballyhoo [ˌbæliˈhuː]n. 招揽生意的广告；大吹大擂 v. 大肆 宣扬；大吹大擂 例 The advertisement specially designed for the company's new products was attended with too much ballyhoo.
[15:50.28]spectrum [ˈspektrəm]n. 谱，光谱，频谱；范围，幅度 搭 solar spectrum 太阳光谱
[15:56.52]evolution [ˌiːvəˈluːʃn]n. 演变，进化；发展 例 The manager is struggling between evolution and revolution in our department.
[16:08.52]exile [ˈeksaɪl]vt. 流放，放逐；使流亡 n. 流放，放逐； 流亡；被流放者，背井离乡者 例 A person who is sent into exile is always someone who has different political ideas. 搭 exile oneself to... 背井离乡去… / send sb. into exile 流放某人
[16:28.08]redirect [ˌriːdəˈrekt]vt. (信件)改寄；使改道；使改变方向 例 Please redirect our mail to the new address.
